  "interpretation": "RQ7 ran 25 attack \u00d7 aggregator cells on the FD001+FD003 Non-IID partition. Baseline (clean + vanilla FedAvg) was RMSE 17.9479. Under attack with no defense the global model degraded to RMSE 84.03 (worst). The best Byzantine-robust aggregator recovered RMSE to 18.40 (within ~1 cycle of the clean baseline). This extends the Yin/Blanchard/Landau family of robust aggregators to four attack types (label-flip, catastrophic gradient scaling, stealthy bounded-scale, backdoor) and to the coordinated Byzantine case (2 of 4 clients malicious), exposing the tolerance limits of each defence.",
